-- Word boundaries: UAX #29 section 4, as the crate implements it in
-- `src/word.rs`.
--
-- `wordEnd` is the crate's forward state machine (`UWordBounds::next`), which
-- reads one word bound from a starting character: it follows the rules that
-- join characters, skips formatting and extending characters (WB4), and backs
-- up when a letter or number fails to follow a mid-word character.
--
-- `unicodeWords` keeps the pieces with a letter or number in them, and for an
-- all-ASCII string uses the crate's faster ASCII segmenter instead, which
-- answers slightly differently in places; it is ported too, so that the
-- answers agree with the crate's.
--
